.TH PRIVACYFOX-APPLY 1 "September 2026" "privacyfox 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
privacyfox-apply \- apply PrivacyFox's hardened profile to your Waterfox install
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B privacyfox-apply
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B privacyfox-apply
finishes the setup that the
.B privacyfox
package's install step can't safely do itself. Installing the package
already drops
.I distribution/policies.json
into Waterfox's system install directory \- that part runs as root,
during
.BR "apt install" ,
and needs no further action.

What it can't do at install time is touch your personal Waterfox
profile: Debian packaging rules don't allow a
.B postinst
maintainer script (which runs as root, with no specific user session)
to write into a user's home directory. That's the one remaining piece
.B privacyfox-apply
does, run once by you, as yourself, with no
.BR sudo .

Specifically, each run:
.IP \(bu 2
Refuses to proceed if Waterfox is currently running, since Waterfox
rewrites
.I user.js
and
.I prefs.js
on exit and would silently overwrite what this command just wrote.
.IP \(bu 2
Locates your default Waterfox profile via
.IR ~/.waterfox/profiles.ini .
.IP \(bu 2
Backs up any existing
.I user.js
in that profile to a timestamped
.I user.js.bak.<timestamp>
file before overwriting it.
.IP \(bu 2
Copies the merged Arkenfox + Betterfox hardening file
.RI ( PrivacyFox.js ,
shipped by the package at
.IR /usr/share/privacyfox/PrivacyFox.js )
into the profile as
.IR user.js .
.IP \(bu 2
Copies
.I userContent.css
into the profile's
.I chrome/
directory, if the package ships one \- purely cosmetic vendor-UI
cleanup, skipped silently if absent.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Applied successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Waterfox was running, no Waterfox profile could be found, or the
.B privacyfox
package's files weren't present at
.IR /usr/share/privacyfox/ .
The error message printed explains which.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/privacyfox/PrivacyFox.js
The hardening file this command copies into your profile.
.TP
.I /usr/share/privacyfox/userContent.css
The optional cosmetic cleanup file, if shipped.
.TP
.I ~/.waterfox/profiles.ini
Read to find your default profile directory. Not written to.
.TP
.I ~/.waterfox/<profile>/user.js
Overwritten with the content of
.I PrivacyFox.js
each run, after a timestamped backup.
.SH NOTES
Safe to re-run at any time, including after
.B "apt upgrade privacyfox"
ships an updated
.IR PrivacyFox.js .
Each run simply refreshes
.I user.js
from whatever the currently installed package contains, backing up
the previous version first.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR waterfox (1),
.I policies.json
at
.IR /usr/lib/waterfox/distribution/policies.json ,
installed by the
.B privacyfox
package itself.
.PP
Full source, credits, and documentation:
.UR https://github.com/rjc3rd/PrivacyFox
.UE
